  ✓ Stage 3: reconstruct semantics/proofs cleanly and execute generated semantics
  ✓ Stage 4: assess claim adequacy and real-program pinning
  ✓ Stage 5: inventory and audit every K declaration and rule
  ✓ Stage 6: create and test a fresh false mutation
  → Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md
